/* Ported verbatim from the production site (deeptech_frontend/src/content/privacy-policy.md). Do not edit wording here without legal review. */
const source: string = "# PRIVACY POLICY & COMPLIANCE FRAMEWORK\n\n**Last Updated:** October 6, 2026  \n**Version:** 2.3\n\nWelcome to ASTEAI (\"ASTEAI,\" \"we,\" \"our,\" or \"us\"), operated under our corporate parent entity, Startrit Infratech Pvt. Ltd. We are committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring complete transparency regarding how we collect, use, disclose, store, and protect your personal information through industry-leading security and quality management frameworks.\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains how ASTEAI collects and processes personal data when you access or use our website (https://asteai.com/), mobile applications, expert marketplace, consultation interfaces, vetting portals, AI-powered tools, and related services (collectively, the \"Services\").\n\nThis Policy tells you what we collect, why, and what you can do about it. Where the law requires your consent for a particular use of your personal data, we ask for it separately and by a clear affirmative action — we do not treat your continued use of the Services as consent for those purposes. Section 19 explains how consent is collected, recorded, and withdrawn. Processing that does not require consent is carried out on the legal bases set out in Section 17.\n\n**Intermediary Status:** ASTEAI operates as an \"intermediary\" as defined under Section 2(1)(w) of the Information Technology Act, 2000, and processes user data in its capacity as an intermediary providing access to a communication system. This Privacy Policy is published in compliance with Rule 3(1) of the Information Technology (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021.\n\n---\n\n## 1. INFORMATION WE COLLECT\n\n### 1.1 Information You Provide Voluntarily\n\n**Account Information:** Full name, email address, phone number, username, encrypted password, and profile photograph.\n\n**Professional Information (Experts):** Resume/CV, education history, certifications, skills, technical expertise, employment history, portfolios, publications, and external workspace or code repository links (e.g., GitHub, GitLab, LinkedIn).\n\n**Business Information (Clients):** Company name, corporate registration data, tax identification numbers (GST/PAN/EIN), project requirements, and service requests.\n\n**Education Verification Data:** College email address, college website, degree level, enrollment status, and education certificates (uploaded to secure storage for verification by authorized administrators).\n\n**Assessment & Multimedia Data:** Video and audio recordings from technical vetting sessions, live AI interview assessment consultations, and code execution walkthroughs. We process these strictly as standard multimedia files to evaluate domain competence and communication skills; we do not extract, generate, or store biometric identifiers or facial geometric templates from these files.\n\n**Communications:** Support requests, internal messages between users, feedback, reviews, and platform consultation requests.\n\n### 1.2 Automatically Collected Information\n\n**Technical Telemetry:** IP address, unique device identifiers, browser information, operating system, language/vernacular settings, session tracking tokens, and diagnostic log data.\n\n**Usage Analytics:** Pages visited, referring/exit URLs, interaction times, and keystroke telemetry indices generated strictly within voluntary technical testing interfaces.\n\n### 1.3 Cookies and Tracking Technologies\n\nWe utilize essential, security, authentication, analytics, performance, and preference cookies through an integrated Cookie Management Center. We do not use invasive tracking technologies that profile users across unrelated third-party websites without consent.\n\n---\n\n## 2. HOW WE USE YOUR INFORMATION\n\nWe use collected information to execute contract obligations, protect our platform integrity, and fulfill legitimate business interests:\n\n**Service Delivery:** Managing accounts, connecting experts with clients based on language/domain preferences, processing transactions, and facilitating milestone payouts.\n\n**Platform Operations & Anti-Bypass Rules:** Improving platform functionality, running automated keyword and pattern-matching scanners on internal chat communications to detect platform abuse, fraud, and disintermediation (moving off-platform to avoid fees).\n\n**Education Verification:** Processing education credentials and certificates submitted by users for manual verification by authorized administrators, and determining verification status displayed on user profiles.\n\n**Legal Compliance:** Meeting cross-border regulatory requirements, enforcing user agreements, and protecting platform security.\n\n**Quality Assurance:** Monitoring service quality, conducting customer satisfaction surveys, and implementing continuous improvement processes.\n\n**Security Monitoring:** Detecting and preventing security incidents, conducting risk assessments, and maintaining audit logs as required by our ISO/IEC 27001-certified Information Security Management System.\n\n---\n\n## 3. AI SYSTEMS AND AUTOMATED PROCESSING\n\nASTEAI utilizes artificial intelligence systems to recommend experts, match clients with professionals, improve search relevance, and optimize platform efficiency.\n\n### 3.1 Core Ethical Commitments\n\n**No External AI Training:** ASTEAI will NOT sell or share private user content, profiles, resumes, or recordings with external AI providers for model training without explicit consent. Any machine learning processing is strictly limited to ASTEAI-operated, secure cloud infrastructure.\n\n**Mandatory Human Oversight:** We will NOT use automated processing as the sole basis for irreversible profile suspensions. All high-stakes automated decisions (such as vetting failures or fraud bans) are subject to mandatory human review.\n\n**Processing Integrity:** AI systems undergo accuracy testing and validation before release and are reviewed when their models or prompts change.\n\n### 3.2 Third-Party AI Service Providers\n\nWhen You use AI-powered features on Our Service (such as project generation, expert search, gig generation, voice input, and language translation), Your data may be processed by the following third-party services:\n\n#### **Amazon Web Services (AWS)**\n\nWe use multiple AWS services to operate Our platform:\n\n- **AWS Bedrock** — Used for AI text generation features including project generation, expert matching recommendations, and content suggestions. Your input prompts are transmitted to AWS Bedrock servers for processing. **By default, AWS does not use Your prompts to train their foundation models.** AWS processes this data in accordance with the [AWS Privacy Notice](https://aws.amazon.com/privacy/). Processing occurs in compliance with AWS's data protection commitments under our Data Processing Agreement.\n\n- **AWS Translate** — Used to translate content across languages on Our platform, enabling multi-language support for expert profiles, project descriptions, and platform interface. Text content You submit may be transmitted to AWS Translate for language processing. AWS processes this data in accordance with the AWS Privacy Notice.\n\n- **AWS EC2** — Our AI services and platform infrastructure run on AWS EC2 servers located in the **Asia Pacific (Mumbai)** region. Your data is processed and temporarily stored on these servers during feature execution. All data at rest is encrypted using AES-256 encryption, and data in transit is protected with TLS 1.3.\n\n#### **Groq**\n\nWe use Groq's API (Whisper model) to process voice input features on Our platform. When You use voice search or voice input for project descriptions or expert search, Your audio data is transmitted to Groq's servers for speech-to-text transcription. Groq processes this data in accordance with their [Privacy Policy](https://groq.com/privacy-policy/). \n\n**Important:** Audio data is not stored by Us beyond what is necessary to complete the transcription. Once transcription is complete, the audio file is immediately discarded from Our systems.\n\n#### **Hugging Face (Embeddings)**\n\nWe use the BAAI/bge-m3 embedding model from Hugging Face for semantic search and expert matching features. **This model runs locally on Our own servers (AWS EC2 in Mumbai region).** When this model processes Your data for search and matching features, Your data does not leave Our infrastructure and is not transmitted to Hugging Face servers. This ensures maximum data privacy for embedding generation.\n\n### 3.3 Data Minimization for AI Features\n\nWe apply the following privacy-protective practices when processing Your data through AI services:\n\n- **Selective Transmission:** Your prompts are transmitted only to the specific service required to fulfill the feature request (e.g., AWS Bedrock for text generation, AWS Translate for language conversion, Groq for voice transcription).\n\n- **Minimal Storage:** We do not store Your raw AI input prompts beyond what is operationally necessary for debugging and service improvement (typically 7-14 days in system logs).\n\n- **Output Retention:** AI-generated outputs (such as project suggestions, expert recommendations) are returned to You and stored only as part of Your account data (e.g., saved project drafts, search history). You can delete this data at any time through account settings.\n\n- **Voice Data Disposal:** Voice audio data is discarded immediately after transcription is complete. We retain only the resulting text transcript if You save the generated content.\n\n- **Local Processing Priority:** Where technically feasible (such as with embedding generation), we run AI models locally on Our infrastructure to avoid external data transmission.\n\n### 3.4 Logging and Monitoring of AI Services\n\nOur platform logs operational data (such as API requests, error messages, system events, and AI service response times) to Docker container logs on Our servers for debugging and service reliability purposes. These logs may contain:\n\n- Metadata about Your interactions with AI features (token counts, response times, error codes)\n- Truncated or hashed versions of prompts for debugging purposes\n- API endpoint usage and performance metrics\n\n**Log Retention:** AI service logs are retained for up to 90 days and are then automatically deleted.\n\n**Future Expansion:** We intend to expand Our logging and monitoring infrastructure in the future, which may include log aggregation services (such as AWS CloudWatch or ELK stack) and alerting systems. This Privacy Policy will be updated to reflect any such changes before they take effect.\n\n### 3.5 Your Control Over AI Processing\n\n- **Opt-Out:** While AI features are integral to Our platform's functionality, You can minimize AI processing by avoiding optional features like voice input and limiting use of AI-generated suggestions.\n\n- **Data Deletion:** You can request deletion of Your account data, which includes all AI-generated content associated with Your account. See Section 13.1 for account deletion procedures.\n\n- **No Training on Your Data:** We do NOT use Your prompts, interactions, or content to train Our own AI models or third-party models without explicit consent through a separate opt-in mechanism.\n\n### 3.6 How Our AI Matching Algorithms Work\n\n**Transparency Commitment:** We believe users deserve to understand how our AI systems make recommendations that affect their opportunities and business connections.\n\n**Expert-Client Matching Process:**\n\nOur AI matching system uses a multi-factor approach to connect clients with the most suitable experts:\n\n1. **Semantic Understanding:** When a client posts a project or searches for an expert, we use natural language processing (via the BAAI/bge-m3 embedding model running on our servers) to understand the core requirements beyond just keyword matching. This means a search for \"machine learning expert\" will also surface experts with related skills like \"deep learning,\" \"neural networks,\" or \"AI model development.\"\n\n2. **Skill Alignment:** The system compares the project requirements against expert profiles, including verified skills, certifications, past project experience, and domain expertise. Each match receives a relevance score based on how closely the expert's capabilities align with the client's needs.\n\n3. **Language & Communication Preferences:** We factor in language proficiency and timezone compatibility to ensure effective communication between clients and experts.\n\n4. **Quality Signals:** The algorithm considers expert ratings, project completion rates, response times, and client satisfaction scores from previous engagements to prioritize reliable professionals.\n\n5. **Diversity & Fairness:** Our system is designed to provide diverse recommendations and avoid over-concentration. We do NOT use protected characteristics (age, gender, ethnicity, religion, location beyond timezone/language matching) as direct factors in ranking experts.\n\n6. **Human Calibration:** Algorithm performance is regularly reviewed by our quality assurance team. If you believe a match recommendation is inaccurate or unfair, you can report it through the platform, and a human reviewer will investigate.\n\n**Project & Gig Generation:**\n\nWhen you use our AI-powered project generation features, the system:\n- Analyzes your input description and expands it with relevant technical requirements, deliverables, and milestones based on patterns learned from successful past projects\n- Suggests realistic timelines and budget ranges based on project complexity\n- Recommends skill requirements that match the project scope\n\n**What the Algorithm Does NOT Do:**\n- Make final hiring decisions (clients always have full control)\n- Automatically reject or suspend experts based solely on AI scoring\n- Use biometric data or facial analysis from video assessments for matching\n- Share your search patterns or preferences with third parties for advertising\n\n**Transparency Limitations:** While we strive for transparency, we cannot disclose the precise mathematical formulas and weights used in our algorithms, as this is proprietary and disclosing it could enable gaming of the system. However, the core principles above govern all our AI decision-making.\n\n---\n\n## 4. INFORMATION SHARING & THIRD-PARTY DISCLOSURES\n\nWe do not sell user personal data. We share information only under the following strict conditions:\n\n**Between Clients and Experts:** Public profiles, verified skill badges, and reviews are visible to clients. Project requirements and corporate profiles are visible to matched experts once an Auto-NDA (Non-Disclosure Agreement) is digitally executed.\n\n**With Cloud Infrastructure Providers:** Core database and compute systems hosted via secured environments (such as Amazon Web Services and Google Cloud Platform) under strict Data Processing Agreements (DPAs) with ISO 27001-certified providers.\n\n**With Escrow & Payment Gateways:** Financial information (bank credentials, credit card numbers, KYC documents) is captured directly by our third-party, PCI-DSS compliant payment gateway, **Razorpay**. ASTEAI processes escrow milestones and ledger entries but never stores raw financial payment credentials on its servers.\n\n### 4.1 Sub-Processors\n\nThe following third parties process personal data on our behalf. Each operates under a Data Processing Agreement and is permitted to process personal data only on our documented instructions.\n\n| Sub-Processor | Purpose | Data Categories | Processing Location |\n|---------------|---------|-----------------|---------------------|\n| **Amazon Web Services (AWS)** | Compute, storage, AI inference (Bedrock), translation, text-to-speech | Account data, content, assessment media, AI prompts | Asia Pacific (Mumbai), with Bedrock inference in the AWS region serving your request |\n| **Supabase** | Managed database, authentication, and file storage (including education certificates) | Account credentials, profile data, uploaded documents | Asia Pacific (Sydney) |\n| **Razorpay** | Payment processing and escrow settlement | Name, contact details, payment instrument data, KYC documents | India |\n| **Groq** | Speech-to-text transcription for voice features | Audio recordings (transient; discarded after transcription) | United States |\n| **Sentry** | Application error monitoring and crash reporting | IP address, user identifier, browser and request headers, stack traces, URL of the page where the error occurred | **United States** |\n| **PostHog** | Product analytics and usage measurement | Pseudonymous device identifier, user identifier once signed in, page views, in-app interaction events, search terms entered in the platform search | United States or EU, per deployment region |\n| **Google LLC (Sign-In / One Tap)** | Federated authentication | Email address, name, profile photograph, Google account identifier | United States |\n| **Termly** | Cookie consent banner and consent preference storage | Consent choices, pseudonymous consent identifier, IP address | United States |\n\n**Cross-Border Note:** Several of the sub-processors above process data outside India. This is permitted under Section 16 of the DPDP Act, which allows transfers except to territories restricted by Central Government notification. Where our infrastructure is described elsewhere in this Policy as India-hosted, that describes our **primary application and database infrastructure**; the error-monitoring, analytics, authentication, and consent services listed above are hosted outside India, and are disclosed here for that reason.\n\nAn up-to-date list of sub-processors is available from privacy@asteai.com. We will give notice of material additions to this list.\n\n**Legal Requirements:** When required to respond to valid subpoenas, court orders, or national security provisions under applicable global laws. ASTEAI complies with lawful requests from authorized government agencies under Section 69 of the IT Act, 2000.\n\n**Education Verification:** Education certificates and credentials are accessible only to authorized ASTEAI administrators for the sole purpose of manual verification. Verified/rejected status is displayed on user profiles, but the underlying certificates are not shared with other users.\n\n---\n\n## 5. DATA RETENTION\n\nWe retain personal information only as long as necessary to provide services, maintain accounts, and satisfy statutory financial or tax obligations.\n\n### 5.1 Retention Periods by Data Category\n\nWhere possible, We apply shorter retention periods and reduce identifiability by deleting, aggregating, or anonymizing data. Unless otherwise stated, the retention periods below are maximum periods (\"up to\") and We may delete or anonymize data sooner when it is no longer needed for the relevant purpose.\n\n| Data Type | Retention Period | Justification |\n|-----------|------------------|---------------|\n| **Account Information** | | |\n| User Accounts (Active) | Duration of account relationship | Contract performance & service delivery |\n| User Accounts (Post-Deletion) | Up to 24 months after account closure | Handle post-termination issues, resolve disputes, fraud prevention |\n| **Expert Verification Data** | | |\n| Video/Audio Assessments | Until account deletion + 90 days | Verification integrity, dispute resolution |\n| Certifications & Credentials | Duration of account relationship | Qualifications validation |\n| Education Certificates | Until account deletion + 90 days | Education verification integrity |\n| **Financial Records** | | |\n| Billing & Escrow Records | Up to 7 years | Corporate and tax law compliance (IRS, Indian IT Act) |\n| Payment Transaction Logs | Up to 7 years | Financial audit requirements |\n| **Communications** | | |\n| Support Tickets & Correspondence | Up to 24 months from ticket closure | Resolve follow-up inquiries, track service quality, defend legal claims |\n| Chat Transcripts (Customer Support) | Up to 24 months | Quality assurance and staff training |\n| Internal Platform Messages | Duration of account relationship + 90 days | Contract performance, dispute resolution |\n| **Technical & Usage Data** | | |\n| Website Analytics (cookies, device IDs) | Up to 24 months from collection | Analyze trends while respecting privacy principles |\n| Server Logs (IP addresses, access times) | Up to 24 months | Security monitoring and troubleshooting |\n| AI Service Logs (prompts, token counts) | Up to 90 days | Debugging and service reliability |\n| **Security Data** | | |\n| Security Incident Logs | Up to 24 months | Security incident investigation & ISO 27001 compliance |\n| Audit Trails (Access Logs) | Up to 24 months | Compliance monitoring and forensic analysis |\n| **Quality Records** | | |\n| Quality Management Documentation | Up to 5 years | Service-quality audit trail |\n| Customer Satisfaction Surveys | Up to 3 years | Service improvement tracking |\n| **Grievance & Compliance Records** | | |\n| Grievance Records | Up to 180 days after resolution | IT Rules 2021 record-keeping obligation |\n| Consent Records | Duration of account relationship + 24 months | Demonstrating valid consent under DPDP Act & GDPR |\n\n### 5.2 Extended Retention Circumstances\n\nWe may retain Personal Data beyond the periods stated above for the following reasons:\n\n- **Legal Obligation:** We are required by law to retain specific data (e.g., financial records for tax authorities, records subject to litigation holds).\n- **Legal Claims:** Data is necessary to establish, exercise, or defend legal claims during active litigation or disputes.\n- **Your Explicit Request:** You ask Us to retain specific information for Your own purposes.\n- **Technical Limitations:** Data exists in encrypted backup systems that are scheduled for routine deletion cycles.\n\nYou may request information about how long We will retain Your specific Personal Data by contacting privacy@asteai.com.\n\n### 5.3 Data Deletion and Anonymization Procedures\n\nWhen retention periods expire, We securely delete or anonymize Personal Data according to the following procedures:\n\n**Deletion:**\n- Personal Data is removed from Our primary production systems and databases\n- Data is overwritten using secure deletion methods to prevent recovery\n- No longer actively processed or accessible to employees\n\n**Backup Retention:**\n- Residual copies may remain in encrypted backups for a limited period consistent with our backup retention schedule (maximum 30 days for incremental backups, 90 days for full backups)\n- Backup copies are not restored except where necessary for security, disaster recovery, or legal compliance\n- Backups containing expired data are securely destroyed according to schedule\n\n**Anonymization:**\n- In some cases, We convert Personal Data into anonymous statistical data that cannot be linked back to You\n- Anonymization is performed using industry-standard techniques (data aggregation, k-anonymity, differential privacy)\n- This anonymized data may be retained indefinitely for research, analytics, and service improvement purposes\n\n**Verification:**\n- Data deletion and anonymization processes are reviewed within our ISO/IEC 27001 internal audit programme\n- Deletion logs are maintained for audit purposes (without storing the deleted content itself)\n\n---\n\n## 6. INFORMATION SECURITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (ISMS)\n\n### 6.1 ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Certification\n\nASTEAI operates an Information Security Management System (ISMS) certified to ISO/IEC 27001:2022. A copy of our certificate, including the certification body and the scope of certification, is available on request from compliance@asteai.com.\n\n**Scope:** The information assets, people, processes, and technology that support the ASTEAI platform, including user data, intellectual property, system infrastructure, and business operations.\n\n**Information Security Policy:** Management-approved policies governing the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of information assets, reviewed at least annually and whenever there is a significant change.\n\n**Risk Management Framework:**\n- Information security risk assessments conducted at least annually and whenever there is a significant change to our systems, suppliers, or services\n- Risk treatment plans with documented controls, recorded in our Statement of Applicability\n- Residual risk accepted by accountable management\n- Ongoing risk monitoring and reassessment\n\n**Asset Management:**\n- Inventory of information assets with assigned owners\n- Classification scheme: Public, Internal, Confidential, Highly Confidential\n- Secure asset handling procedures throughout the asset lifecycle\n\n**Access Control:**\n- Principle of least privilege applied across production systems\n- Multi-factor authentication (MFA) required for administrative access\n- Documented user access provisioning and de-provisioning procedures\n- Periodic access reviews of privileged and production access\n- Segregation of duties for critical functions where team size allows\n\n**Cryptography:**\n- Encryption of data at rest (AES-256) provided by our database and cloud infrastructure providers\n- TLS 1.2 or higher for data in transit\n- Cryptographic keys managed through our cloud providers' managed key services; application secrets are held outside source code\n- Key rotation and revocation procedures\n\n**Physical and Environmental Security:**\n- ASTEAI does not operate its own data centres. Production systems are hosted by the cloud providers listed in Section 4.1, whose data centres hold ISO/IEC 27001 certification and provide physical and environmental controls\n- Secure handling and disposal of company devices and physical media\n\n**Operations Security:**\n- Change management with code review and approval before production deployment\n- Capacity and performance monitoring\n- Malware protection on company endpoints\n- Automated database backups, with periodic restoration testing\n- Secure configuration baselines for production systems\n\n**Communications Security:**\n- Separation of production, staging, and development environments\n- Rate limiting and abuse protection on public interfaces\n- Regular vulnerability scanning of application dependencies, and periodic penetration testing\n\n**Threat Intelligence & Security Monitoring:**\n- Monitoring of CERT-In advisories and vendor security bulletins relevant to our technology stack\n- Application error and anomaly monitoring with automated alerting\n- Prioritised patching of critical vulnerabilities\n\n**Supplier Security:**\n- Security assessment of third-party processors before engagement\n- Data Processing Agreements (DPAs) with our processors\n- Annual review of critical suppliers\n\n**Incident Management:**\n- Documented incident response procedure with defined roles and severity levels\n- Notification of reportable incidents to CERT-In within 6 hours, and to affected users and the Data Protection Board of India as required by law (see Section 13)\n- Root cause analysis, corrective action, and post-incident review\n\n**Business Continuity:**\n- Business impact analysis and business continuity plan, reviewed at least annually\n- Defined recovery time and recovery point objectives for critical services\n- Disaster recovery testing at least annually\n\n**Compliance:**\n- Internal ISMS audits at planned intervals, covering the full ISMS at least once a year\n- Management review of ISMS performance at least annually\n- Annual external surveillance audits by our certification body, and full recertification every three years\n- Monitoring of compliance with applicable legal and regulatory requirements\n\n---\n\n## 7. DATA SECURITY CONTROLS\n\nIn addition to our ISMS, ASTEAI applies the following controls. ASTEAI does not currently hold a SOC 2 report.\n\n### 7.1 Security\n\n- Encryption of data in transit (TLS 1.2 or higher) and at rest (AES-256)\n- Rate limiting, input validation, and dependency vulnerability scanning on application and API boundaries\n- Least-privilege employee access controls with confidentiality obligations\n- Automated security alerting\n- Periodic penetration testing\n- Secure software development practices, including code review before release\n\n### 7.2 Availability\n\n**Service Availability:** We target high availability for core platform services. Contractual service levels, where offered, are set out in the customer's Master Services Agreement or order form.\n\n**Infrastructure Resilience:**\n- Managed cloud infrastructure with health monitoring and automated alerting\n- Automated database backups maintained by our database provider\n- Capacity monitoring and scaling of application services\n\n### 7.3 Processing Integrity\n\n- Input validation and sanitization to prevent injection attacks\n- Transaction logging and audit trails for financial operations\n- Error monitoring and alerting\n\n### 7.4 Confidentiality\n\n- Data classification policy with handling requirements\n- Confidential data encrypted at rest and in transit\n- Confidentiality agreements for all employees and contractors\n- Secure data destruction for decommissioned systems\n\n### 7.5 Privacy\n\nPrivacy controls as detailed throughout this policy, including:\n- Privacy by design in system development\n- Data minimization and purpose limitation\n- User consent management with granular controls\n- Privacy impact assessments for new high-risk processing\n- Privacy and security awareness training for employees\n\n---\n\n## 8. SERVICE QUALITY\n\nASTEAI is committed to delivering reliable, user-centric marketplace services. ASTEAI does not currently hold ISO 9001 certification.\n\n**Our commitments:**\n- Measuring customer satisfaction through post-transaction feedback and support-ticket analysis\n- Investigating service failures, identifying root causes, and tracking corrective actions to completion\n- Reviewing service-quality metrics and user feedback with management on a regular basis\n- Maintaining version-controlled policies and procedures with approval before publication\n\n---\n\n## 9. ENVIRONMENTAL COMMITMENT\n\nASTEAI recognizes the environmental impact of digital infrastructure. ASTEAI does not currently hold ISO 14001 certification.\n\n**Our commitments:**\n- Preferring cloud providers and regions with renewable-energy commitments\n- Deleting expired data on schedule (Section 5) and optimizing queries, caching, and storage to avoid unnecessary computation\n- Using virtual meetings to reduce travel-related emissions\n- Complying with applicable environmental law, including responsible e-waste disposal of company devices\n\n---\n\n## 10. YOUR PRIVACY RIGHTS (GLOBAL REGULATORY ALIGNMENT)\n\n### 10.1 India Compliance (DPDP Act 2023)\n\n**Data Fiduciary:** Startrit Infratech Pvt. Ltd. (operating ASTEAI) is the **Data Fiduciary** in respect of personal data processed through the Services, and determines the purposes and means of that processing. Where we engage vendors to process personal data on our instructions, those vendors act as **Data Processors** under written contract.\n\nFor users residing within India, under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (\"DPDP Act\"):\n\n**Data Principal Rights:**\n- You have the right to access, correct, or erase your digital personal data\n- You may withdraw consent for processing where consent is the legal basis\n- You may nominate another individual to exercise your rights in the event of death or incapacity\n- You have the right to redress grievances by contacting our designated Grievance Officer (see Section 10.1A below) before escalating concerns to the Data Protection Board of India\n\n**Section 9 — Protection of Children and Persons with Disability:**\n- ASTEAI does not knowingly process the personal data of children (persons below **18 years of age**) without verifiable consent from a parent or lawful guardian\n- We do not undertake tracking or behavioural monitoring of children, or targeted advertising directed at children\n- We do not process the personal data of children in any manner likely to cause a detrimental effect on their well-being\n- The protections afforded to children under Section 9 apply equally to persons with disabilities who have a lawful guardian, where processing requires the consent of such guardian\n- We implement age-gating mechanisms during account registration to verify minimum age requirements\n- If we become aware that the personal data of a child has been processed without verifiable parental consent, we shall delete such data within 72 hours\n- We do not process the personal data of children for profiling, automated decision-making, or any processing that could reasonably be expected to cause significant harm\n\n**Certain Legitimate Uses (Section 7):**\n\nThe DPDP Act does not recognise \"legitimate interests\" as a ground for processing. Where we process the personal data of users in India without separately obtained consent, we rely only on the enumerated \"certain legitimate uses\" in Section 7 of the DPDP Act, namely:\n- Where the Data Principal has voluntarily provided the data for a specified purpose and has not indicated an objection to its use for that purpose\n- For compliance with any judgment, decree, or order of any court or tribunal\n- For responding to a medical emergency involving a threat to life or immediate health risk\n- For employment-related purposes, including safeguarding the employer from loss or liability\n- For purposes related to public interest as prescribed by the Central Government\n\nProcessing that does not fall within Section 7 is carried out only on the basis of your consent, obtained as described in Section 19 (Consent Management).\n\n### 10.1A Grievance Officer (India — IT Rules 2021 & DPDP Act)\n\nIn compliance with Rule 3(2) of the IT Rules 2021 and the DPDP Act, ASTEAI appoints:\n\n**Grievance Officer:**\n- **Name:** Rahul Yash Vardhan\n- **Email:** grievance@asteai.com\n- **Phone:** +91 866 727 5560\n- **Address:** Startrit Infratech Pvt. Ltd., Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India - 600095\n- **Working Hours:** Monday to Friday, 10:00 AM to 6:00 PM IST\n\n**Process:**\n- Submit a grievance by email to grievance@asteai.com or through the Platform's \"Report\" feature\n- Acknowledgment within 24 hours of receipt\n- Resolution within 15 days from the date of receipt (per IT Rules 2021)\n- Content takedown, where applicable, within 36 hours\n- If unsatisfied, you may escalate to the Data Protection Board of India\n\n**Scope:** The Grievance Officer handles complaints relating to privacy violations, unauthorised data processing, content that violates our Terms, IP infringement, platform misuse, and any violation of applicable Indian law.\n\n**Record Keeping:** Grievance records are retained for 180 days after resolution, as required under the IT Rules 2021.\n\n### 10.2 European Union Compliance (GDPR)\n\nFor users in the EEA, UK, and Switzerland, we process data under the following lawful bases:\n\n**Lawful Bases:**\n- **Consent:** Marketing communications, optional data processing\n- **Contract Performance:** Account management, service delivery, payment processing\n- **Legal Obligation:** Tax compliance, fraud prevention, regulatory reporting\n- **Legitimate Interests:** Platform security, fraud detection, service improvement\n\n**Your GDPR Rights:**\n- **Right to Access:** Obtain confirmation of processing and a copy of your personal data\n- **Right to Rectification:** Correct inaccurate or incomplete personal data\n- **Right to Erasure (\"Right to be Forgotten\"):** Request deletion of your personal data\n- **Right to Restriction:** Limit processing in certain circumstances\n- **Right to Data Portability:** Receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format\n- **Right to Object:** Object to processing based on legitimate interests or direct marketing\n- **Right to Withdraw Consent:** Withdraw consent at any time where processing is based on consent\n- **Right to Lodge a Complaint:** File a complaint with your local Data Protection Authority\n- **Right Not to be Subject to Automated Decisions:** Object to decisions based solely on automated processing, including profiling, which produce legal or similarly significant effects\n\n**International Data Transfers:**\n- Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) for transfers outside the EEA\n- Supplementary measures including encryption and access controls\n- Transfer Impact Assessments (TIA) for high-risk transfers\n\n**Data Protection Officer Contact:** dpo@asteai.com\n\n**EU Representative:** For users in the EEA, our EU representative for GDPR matters can be contacted at eu-representative@asteai.com.\n\n### 10.3 United States Compliance (CCPA/CPRA)\n\nCalifornia residents have the following rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA):\n\n**Your California Rights:**\n- **Right to Know:** Request disclosure of personal information collected, used, and shared\n- **Right to Delete:** Request deletion of personal information\n- **Right to Correct:** Request correction of inaccurate personal information\n- **Right to Opt-Out:** Opt-out of the sale or sharing of personal information\n- **Right to Limit Use of Sensitive Personal Information:** Limit use and disclosure of sensitive PI\n- **Right to Non-Discrimination:** Not receive discriminatory treatment for exercising privacy rights\n\n**Our Commitments:**\n- ASTEAI does NOT \"sell\" or \"share\" personal information as defined by CCPA/CPRA\n- We do NOT use or disclose sensitive personal information beyond what is necessary to provide services\n- Response timeline: Acknowledgment within 10 days, response within 45 days (extendable by 45 days)\n\n**Authorized Agent:** You may designate an authorized agent to submit requests on your behalf. We require written authorization and verification of identity.\n\n**California Do Not Track:** We honor Global Privacy Control (GPC) signals.\n\n### 10.4 Other US State Privacy Laws\n\nFor residents of Virginia (VCDPA), Colorado (CPA), Connecticut (CTDPA), and Utah (UCPA), you have similar rights to those provided under CCPA, including rights to access, delete, correct, and opt-out of targeted advertising and profiling.\n\n### 10.4A Other Jurisdictions\n\n**Brazil (LGPD):** Users in Brazil may exercise rights under the Lei Geral de Proteção de Dados, including access, correction, anonymization, portability, and deletion.\n\n**Singapore (PDPA):** Users in Singapore have the right to access and correct personal data, withdraw consent, and request data portability under the Personal Data Protection Act.\n\n### 10.5 Exercising Your Rights\n\n**How to Submit a Request:**\n- Email: privacy@asteai.com\n- Consent & Communication Preferences: https://asteai.com/consent-preferences\n- California Opt-Out Requests: https://asteai.com/do-not-sell-my-info\n- Account Settings: Self-service tools for access, correction, and deletion\n\n**Verification Process:**\n- We verify your identity using account credentials or multi-factor authentication\n- For high-risk requests (deletion, sensitive data access), additional verification may be required\n- We do not require account creation to submit privacy requests\n\n**Response Timeline:**\n- Acknowledgment: Within 24-72 hours\n- Fulfillment: Within 30-45 days depending on jurisdiction\n- Extensions: We will notify you if additional time is needed\n\n**Appeals Process:**\n- If you are unsatisfied with our response, you may appeal within 30 days\n- Appeals are reviewed by our Data Protection Officer\n- Response to appeals within 30-45 days\n- You retain the right to lodge a complaint with applicable regulatory authorities\n\n### 10.6 Accessibility & Privacy Rights for All Users\n\nASTEAI is committed to ensuring that individuals with disabilities can exercise their privacy rights and access our services with dignity and independence.\n\n**Accessible Privacy Controls:**\n\n- **Screen Reader Compatibility:** Our privacy portal, account settings, and consent management interfaces are designed to be compatible with popular screen readers (JAWS, NVDA, VoiceOver)\n- **Keyboard Navigation:** All privacy-related functions can be accessed and operated using keyboard-only navigation without requiring a mouse\n- **Alternative Formats:** Upon request, we provide this Privacy Policy and related documentation in alternative formats including:\n  - Large print PDF\n  - Plain text format\n  - Audio recording\n  - Simplified language version\n- **Visual Design:** Our privacy interfaces use high-contrast color schemes, resizable text, and clear visual hierarchy to assist users with visual impairments\n- **Captions & Transcripts:** Where video content is used (such as in our vetting process tutorials or privacy training materials), we provide closed captions and text transcripts\n\n**Assisted Privacy Requests:**\n\nIf you require assistance exercising your privacy rights due to a disability, we provide:\n\n- **Phone Support:** Call our dedicated accessibility support line during business hours where trained staff can assist you with privacy requests\n- **Email Assistance:** Send requests to accessibility@asteai.com, and we will work with you to accommodate your needs\n- **Authorized Representatives:** We facilitate the appointment of authorized representatives (family members, caregivers, or legal guardians) to exercise privacy rights on your behalf\n- **Extended Response Time Requests:** If you need additional time to review information or make decisions about privacy choices, we will accommodate reasonable extension requests\n\n**Accessibility in Data Processing:**\n\n- **Consent Mechanisms:** Our consent forms avoid complex interfaces that may be challenging for users with cognitive disabilities. We use clear, simple language and provide \"I agree\" / \"I decline\" options without hidden defaults\n- **Multi-Modal Communication:** We offer multiple ways to contact us (email, phone, web forms, postal mail) recognizing that different users have different accessibility needs\n- **No Discrimination:** We do NOT make privacy protections contingent on specific interaction methods. Whether you contact us by phone, email, assistive technology, or through a representative, you receive the same privacy rights and protections\n\n**Feedback on Accessibility:**\n\nIf you encounter accessibility barriers in exercising your privacy rights or accessing privacy-related information, please contact us at accessibility@asteai.com. We commit to:\n- Responding within 48 hours\n- Working with you to identify alternative solutions\n- Implementing improvements to prevent similar barriers for other users\n- Documenting accessibility issues and remediation in our compliance tracking system\n\n**Compliance Standards:**\n\nOur accessibility practices are informed by:\n- Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 Level AA\n- Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) requirements\n- European Accessibility Act (EAA)\n- Section 508 of the Rehabilitation Act (US)\n\nWe conduct annual accessibility audits of our privacy interfaces and remediate identified issues within 90 days of discovery.\n\n---\n\n## 11. CHILDREN'S PRIVACY\n\n### 11.1 Minimum Age\n\nASTEAI is strictly intended for corporate entities and professional individuals. **Our Service does not address anyone under the age of 18.** We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from anyone under the age of 18.\n\n**Age Verification:** During account registration, users must affirmatively confirm they are at least 18 years of age. We implement age-gating and date-of-birth verification at the point of registration.\n\n### 11.2 DPDP Act Section 9 Compliance (Children and Persons with Disability)\n\nIn specific compliance with Section 9 of the DPDP Act, 2023:\n\n- We do not knowingly process the personal data of any person under the age of 18 without verifiable consent from a parent or lawful guardian\n- We do not process the personal data of children for tracking, behavioural monitoring, or targeted advertising\n- We do not process personal data in any manner likely to cause a detrimental effect on the well-being of a child\n- The protections under this section apply equally to persons with disabilities who have lawful guardians, where processing requires guardian consent\n- We implement technical measures (date-of-birth verification, affirmative age confirmation) to prevent the collection of children's data\n\n**Verifiable Parental Consent:** Where we must rely on consent and your jurisdiction requires parental or guardian consent, we obtain it before collecting or using that information. Verifiable consent mechanisms include email verification from a parent or guardian, signed consent forms, or video verification.\n\n### 11.3 Discovery of a Minor's Data\n\nIf we discover that we have inadvertently collected personal information from a minor, we will:\n\n1. Immediately cease processing such information\n2. Delete the information from our systems within 72 hours\n3. Notify the account holder (if contact information is available)\n4. Take steps to prevent future collection from that individual\n5. Record the incident internally as a data protection event\n\nIf you believe we have collected information from a minor, please contact us immediately at privacy@asteai.com.\n\n---\n\n## 12. INTERNATIONAL DATA TRANSFERS\n\nInformation may be processed and stored in cross-border server clusters where ASTEAI's infrastructure sub-processors operate, including but not limited to the United States, European Union, and India.\n\n**Transfer Mechanisms:**\n- **Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs):** EU Commission-approved SCCs for EEA data transfers\n- **Data Processing Agreements (DPAs):** Binding agreements with all data processors\n- **Supplementary Measures:** Encryption, access controls, data minimization\n- **Transfer Impact Assessments (TIA):** Assessment of legal protections in destination countries\n- **Adequacy Decisions:** Reliance on EU adequacy decisions where applicable\n\n**Data Localization Compliance:**\n- Sensitive data for Indian users stored within India where required by local law\n- Compliance with data localization requirements in applicable jurisdictions\n\n**DPDP Act — Cross-Border Transfers:** Section 16 of the DPDP Act permits the transfer of personal data outside India except to territories that the Central Government restricts by notification. We monitor such notifications and will cease transfers to any restricted territory. Sector-specific localisation requirements (such as those issued by the Reserve Bank of India for payment data) continue to apply and are observed in addition to the DPDP Act.\n\n---\n\n## 13. ACCOUNT SECURITY, DELETION & INCIDENT RESPONSE\n\n### 13.0 How We Will and Will Not Contact You (Anti-Phishing)\n\nFraudulent messages impersonating recruiters, clients, and platform staff are the most common threat to users of any talent marketplace. Please read this section carefully.\n\n**ASTEAI will NEVER ask you for:**\n- Your password — not by email, phone, chat, SMS, or in any support conversation\n- A one-time password (OTP), 2FA code, or authenticator code. Anyone asking you to read out or forward a code is attempting to take over your account\n- Full card number, CVV, UPI PIN, or net-banking credentials. Payments are collected only through our payment gateway's own checkout\n- Remote access to your device, or installation of screen-sharing or \"verification\" software\n- A fee to be hired, to release a payout, to unlock an account, or to receive a certificate other than through the published in-platform purchase flow\n\n**Other things to know:**\n- Official email from ASTEAI comes only from an `@asteai.com` or `@startrit.com` address. We cannot prevent a sender from forging a display name — check the full address, not the name shown\n- We will never ask you to move a hiring conversation to an external messaging app to complete \"verification\"\n- An offer of employment that arrives before any interview, or that requires you to purchase equipment through a specified vendor, should be treated as fraudulent\n- Links in our emails will point to `asteai.com`. When in doubt, do not click — type the address yourself and sign in directly\n\n**Report suspected phishing or impersonation to security@asteai.com.** Include the sender's full address, message headers if available, and any links, without clicking them. If you have already entered credentials, change your password immediately and follow Section 13.0B.\n\n### 13.0A Your Security Responsibilities\n\nProtecting your account is a shared responsibility. You agree to:\n\n- **Keep credentials secret.** Do not disclose your password, OTP, or 2FA codes to anyone, including anyone claiming to be ASTEAI staff\n- **Use a strong, unique password.** Do not reuse a password from another service. We recommend a password manager\n- **Enable two-factor authentication** where offered, at Settings → Security\n- **Do not share your account.** Each account is personal to one individual. Do not let another person use your credentials, and do not use someone else's. Company administrators must issue individual sub-accounts to their personnel rather than sharing one login\n- **Secure your devices.** Use a screen lock, keep your operating system and browser updated, and avoid signing in on shared or public computers. If you must, sign out fully afterwards\n- **Sign out of sessions you no longer use**, particularly on devices you do not control\n- **Verify counterparties** before sending money, work product, or personal documents, and keep project communication and payment on-platform, where it is covered by our dispute process\n- **Notify us promptly** if you suspect unauthorised access, at security@asteai.com\n\nYou are responsible for activity carried out under your credentials, except to the extent it results from our own failure. Sharing credentials, or ignoring a known compromise, may limit our ability to help you recover the account or reverse transactions.\n\n### 13.0B If Your Account Is Compromised or Your Device Is Lost\n\nIf you believe someone else has accessed your account, or a device with an active session has been lost or stolen:\n\n**Immediate steps you can take:**\n1. Change your password at Settings → Security, or via **Forgot Password** if you have been locked out. Changing your password terminates other active sessions\n2. Review and revoke active sessions and connected devices at Settings → Security\n3. Enable two-factor authentication if it is not already on\n4. Check your profile, payout details, and bank information for unauthorised changes — altering payout details is the most common objective of an account takeover\n5. Email **security@asteai.com** with the approximate time you lost access and anything unusual you noticed\n\n**What we will do:**\n- **Acknowledge your report within 24 hours**, and treat suspected account takeover as a priority incident\n- Lock the account on request, or on our own initiative where we detect a serious risk, to prevent further damage\n- Force termination of all active sessions and require re-authentication\n- Suspend pending payout changes and outgoing transactions while we investigate\n- Provide you with the sign-in history we hold for the affected period\n- Restore access once your identity is verified, and tell you what we found\n\n**If you cannot access your registered email**, contact security@asteai.com from any address and state that you have lost access to your registered email. We will verify your identity by other means before making any change. We will never restore an account to a new email address on the strength of an email request alone.\n\n### 13.0C Authentication and Session Management\n\nWe offer the following ways to sign in and protect an account:\n\n- **Email and password**, with passwords stored only as salted one-way hashes — we cannot retrieve or tell you your password\n- **Google Sign-In / One Tap** federated authentication. Where you sign in with Google, we receive your email address, name, profile photograph, and Google account identifier; we never receive your Google password\n- **One-time passcodes (OTP)** sent to your registered email or phone for verification of sensitive actions\n- **Two-factor authentication (2FA)** for accounts that enable it\n\n**What we retain and for how long:**\n\n| Authentication data | Retention |\n|---------------------|-----------|\n| Password hash | Duration of the account; replaced on each change |\n| Session and refresh tokens | Until expiry, sign-out, password change, or session revocation |\n| OTP codes | Short-lived; invalidated on use or expiry |\n| 2FA recovery codes | Until regenerated by you |\n| Sign-in history (time, IP address, device, outcome) | Up to 24 months, for security investigation |\n\n**Session handling:** Sessions expire after a period of inactivity and on token expiry. Changing your password or revoking sessions terminates existing sessions on other devices. Concurrent sessions on multiple devices are permitted, and each can be reviewed and revoked individually at Settings → Security. Sign-in attempts are rate-limited, and repeated failures may temporarily lock an account to prevent brute-force attacks.\n\nNote that the multi-factor authentication described in Section 6.1 applies to **ASTEAI's own administrative staff** accessing internal systems. This section describes the controls available to **you** on your own account.\n\n### 13.1 Account Deletion\n\nUsers can request permanent account deletion via:\n- Account Settings → Delete Account\n- Support: supportasteai@startrit.com\n- Privacy Requests: privacy@asteai.com\n\n**Deletion Process:**\n1. Identity verification required\n2. 7-day cooling-off period (cancellable by user)\n3. Profile visibility removed immediately upon confirmation\n4. Personal data expunged or anonymized within 7 business days\n5. Retention of specific data for legal obligations:\n   - Financial records: 7 years (tax law compliance)\n   - Fraud investigation data: As required by law enforcement\n   - Dispute resolution records: Until resolution + applicable statute of limitations\n\n**Data Provided to Third Parties:**\n- We will notify clients/experts with whom you had transactions\n- We cannot delete data independently controlled by third parties (you must contact them directly)\n\n### 13.2 Data Breach & Incident Response\n\n**Incident Response Framework (ISO 27035):**\n\n**Phase 1: Detection & Triage (0-1 hour)**\n- Automated monitoring and alerting via SIEM\n- Security Operations Center (SOC) initial assessment\n- Incident severity classification (P0-P4)\n\n**Phase 2: Containment (1-4 hours)**\n- Isolate affected systems to prevent further compromise\n- Preserve forensic evidence\n- Activate incident response team\n\n**Phase 3: Investigation (4-24 hours)**\n- Root cause analysis\n- Scope determination (what data, how many users)\n- Assessment of security control failures\n- Documentation of timeline and impact\n\n**Phase 4: Notification**\n- **Affected Users (India — DPDP Act):** Where the breach affects users in India, we notify **every affected Data Principal without delay**, in their own interest. This obligation is **not** subject to a risk threshold — we do not withhold notice on the basis that we have assessed the breach as low-risk.\n- **Affected Users (other jurisdictions):** Notification within 72 hours of confirmation where the breach is likely to result in a risk to your rights and freedoms.\n- **Regulatory Authorities:**\n  - **India — Data Protection Board:** Intimation without delay, and in any event within **72 hours** of becoming aware of the breach, including the nature, extent, timing and likely consequences of the breach and the remedial measures taken\n  - **India — CERT-In:** Within **6 hours** of noticing or being brought to notice of a reportable cyber security incident (per CERT-In Directions, 28 April 2022)\n  - **GDPR:** 72 hours to the lead supervisory authority where the breach poses a risk to data subjects\n  - **US States:** Per applicable state breach notification laws\n- **Notification Method:** Email, platform dashboard alert, and dedicated breach notification page\n- **Notification Content:** Nature of the breach, data affected, steps taken, and recommended user actions\n\n**Phase 5: Remediation & Recovery**\n- Implementation of additional security controls\n- Affected systems restored from clean backups\n- Password resets and re-authentication as needed\n- Offer of credit monitoring services for financial data breaches (where applicable)\n\n**Phase 6: Post-Incident Review**\n- Lessons learned documentation\n- Update to incident response procedures\n- Security control improvements\n- Report to senior management and board\n\n**User Support:**\n- Dedicated breach response hotline and email\n- FAQ and guidance documentation\n- Individual consultation for high-risk affected users\n\n---\n\n## 14. TRAINING, AWARENESS & GOVERNANCE\n\n### 14.1 Employee Training\n\nAll ASTEAI employees, contractors, and vendors with access to personal data undergo:\n\n- **Onboarding Security Training:** Within first week of employment\n- **Annual Privacy & Security Refresher:** Mandatory completion\n- **Role-Specific Training:**\n  - Developers: Secure coding, OWASP Top 10\n  - Support Staff: Data handling, customer privacy\n  - Administrators: Access control, incident response\n- **Phishing Simulation Tests:** Quarterly\n- **Compliance Training:** GDPR, CCPA, ISO standards\n- **Training Tracking:** Completion records maintained for audit purposes\n\n### 14.2 Governance Structure\n\n**Data Protection Officer (DPO):**\n- Independent oversight of data protection compliance\n- Monitors GDPR, DPDPA, and other privacy law compliance\n- Point of contact for supervisory authorities\n- Conducts Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIA)\n- Reports directly to executive management\n\n**Information Security Officer (ISO):**\n- Oversees ISMS implementation and maintenance\n- Conducts risk assessments and security audits\n- Manages security incident response\n- Reports to CTO and Board\n\n**ISMS Management Representative:**\n- Maintains the ISMS documentation and Statement of Applicability\n- Coordinates internal audits and external certification audits\n- Facilitates management reviews\n- Tracks corrective actions and continual improvement initiatives\n\n**Compliance Committee:**\n- Cross-functional team (Legal, Security, Engineering, Operations)\n- Quarterly meetings to review compliance posture\n- Approval of policy updates\n- Escalation forum for compliance issues\n\n### 14.3 Third-Party Oversight\n\n**Vendor Risk Management:**\n- Pre-engagement security and privacy assessments\n- Annual vendor reviews and audit rights\n- Incident notification requirements in contracts\n- Termination assistance and data return provisions\n\n**Audit Rights:**\n- Customers may request a copy of our ISO/IEC 27001 certificate\n- Enterprise clients may conduct security questionnaires\n- Audit provisions in our customer Data Processing Agreement (available at https://asteai.com/dpa)\n\n---\n\n## 15. PRIVACY BY DESIGN & DATA PROTECTION IMPACT ASSESSMENTS\n\n### 15.1 Privacy by Design Principles\n\nASTEAI embeds privacy into system design and business practices through:\n\n1. **Proactive not Reactive:** Privacy measures implemented from project inception\n2. **Privacy as Default:** Maximum privacy settings applied by default\n3. **Privacy Embedded into Design:** Privacy integral to system architecture\n4. **Full Functionality:** Positive-sum approach, no false trade-offs\n5. **End-to-End Security:** Protection throughout data lifecycle\n6. **Visibility and Transparency:** Clear communication and openness\n7. **User-Centric:** Empowerment of users with control over their data\n\n### 15.2 Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIA)\n\nDPIAs conducted for:\n- New processing activities involving high risk to individuals\n- Use of new technologies (AI, biometrics, profiling)\n- Large-scale processing of sensitive data\n- Systematic monitoring of public areas\n\n**DPIA Process:**\n1. Description of processing operations and purposes\n2. Assessment of necessity and proportionality\n3. Identification of risks to individuals' rights and freedoms\n4. Measures to address risks\n5. Consultation with DPO\n6. Consultation with supervisory authority if high residual risk\n\n---\n\n## 16. COOKIES & TRACKING TECHNOLOGIES (DETAILED)\n\n### 16.1 Types of Cookies We Use\n\n**Strictly Necessary Cookies (Always Active):**\n- Session authentication tokens\n- Security and fraud prevention\n- Load balancing and routing\n- Cookie consent preferences\n\n**Performance & Analytics Cookies (Opt-in):**\n- **PostHog** — product analytics: page views, in-app interaction events (clicks, form interactions, scroll depth), search terms entered in the platform search, session duration, and A/B experiment assignment. Once you sign in, these events are associated with your user identifier.\n- **Sentry** — error and crash reporting, which records the page on which an error occurred together with your IP address and browser details\n- Platform usage metrics and performance monitoring\n- A/B testing and feature optimization\n- Retention: Up to 24 months\n\n**Functional Cookies (Opt-in):**\n- Language and region preferences\n- UI customization settings\n- Accessibility preferences\n\n**Marketing Cookies (Opt-in):**\n- LinkedIn, Google Ads conversion tracking (for business-to-business marketing only)\n- Retargeting for abandoned consultation requests\n- Attribution for marketing campaign effectiveness\n\n### 16.2 Cookie Management\n\n**Cookie Consent Management:**\n- Our cookie consent banner and preference centre are operated by **Termly**, a third-party consent management provider\n- Granular consent options are available at any time through the \"Cookie Preferences\" link in the site footer, or at [Consent Preferences](https://asteai.com/consent-preferences)\n- Consent preferences stored for 12 months\n- Re-consent prompted upon policy changes\n\n**Third-Party Cookies and Scripts:**\n- We do not allow third-party **advertising** networks, and we do not run retargeting or ad-conversion pixels\n- We do use third-party **analytics, error-monitoring, authentication, and payment** scripts, which are named in Section 4.1. These are not advertising services, but they are third parties and they do receive data about your use of the Services\n- **Google Sign-In / One Tap** loads a Google-hosted script (`accounts.google.com/gsi/client`) on pages where signing in is offered. This lets Google know you visited a page presenting a Google sign-in prompt, whether or not you sign in. It is used only for authentication — not for advertising or cross-site profiling by ASTEAI\n- We do not combine analytics data with third-party data brokers, and we do not track you across unrelated websites\n\n**Browser Controls:**\n- Instructions for cookie management in major browsers provided\n- Support for Do Not Track (DNT) and Global Privacy Control (GPC) signals\n\n---\n\n## 17. SPECIFIC PROCESSING ACTIVITIES & LEGAL BASES\n\nThe GDPR and the DPDP Act do not share the same set of lawful bases. In particular, **the DPDP Act has no \"legitimate interests\" ground.** For users in India, any activity that relies on legitimate interests under the GDPR must instead rest either on your consent or on one of the enumerated \"certain legitimate uses\" in Section 7 of the DPDP Act. The table below states both bases separately so the difference is explicit.\n\n| Processing Activity | Data Categories | Legal Basis (GDPR) | Legal Basis (DPDP Act, India) | Purpose |\n|---------------------|-----------------|-------------------|-------------------------------|---------|\n| Account Creation | Name, email, password | Contract Performance | S.7(a) — voluntarily provided for this purpose | Provide marketplace services |\n| Expert Verification | Resume, certifications, video assessments | Contract Performance | S.7(a) — voluntarily provided for this purpose | Verify qualifications and expertise |\n| Education Verification | College email, degree level, certificates | Contract Performance | S.7(a) — voluntarily provided for this purpose | Verify education credentials |\n| Client-Expert Matching | Skills, project requirements, language preferences | Legitimate Interest | **Consent** (no legitimate-interest equivalent) | Connect clients with suitable experts |\n| Payment Processing | Bank details, tax IDs | Contract Performance & Legal Obligation | S.7(a) and S.7(b) — legal/regulatory compliance | Process payments and comply with tax law |\n| Platform Security | IP address, device ID, logs | Legitimate Interest | **Consent** obtained at registration (no legitimate-interest equivalent) | Prevent fraud and maintain security |\n| Marketing Communications | Email, communication preferences | Consent | **Consent** (separately obtained, withdrawable) | Send newsletters and promotional content |\n| Customer Support | Support tickets, chat transcripts | Contract Performance | S.7(a) — voluntarily provided for this purpose | Resolve issues and provide assistance |\n| Analytics & Improvement | Usage data, performance metrics | Legitimate Interest | **Consent** (opt-in; see Section 16.2) | Improve platform functionality |\n| Grievance Handling | Complaint details, correspondence, identity data | Legal Obligation | S.7(b) — compliance with IT Rules 2021 | Investigate and resolve grievances |\n| Legal Compliance | All relevant data | Legal Obligation | S.7(b) — compliance with law, court order, or judgment | Comply with regulatory requirements |\n\n---\n\n## 18. DATA SUBJECT RIGHTS REGISTER\n\nASTEAI maintains a Data Subject Rights Register tracking:\n- Requests received (access, deletion, rectification, portability, objection)\n- Request type and date received\n- Verification method used\n- Response date and outcome\n- Appeals and escalations\n\n**Statistics (Published Annually):**\n- Number of requests by type and jurisdiction\n- Average response time\n- Percentage of requests fulfilled\n- Common request reasons and trends\n\n---\n\n## 19. CONSENT MANAGEMENT\n\n### 19.1 Consent Collection\n\nWhere we rely on your consent, that consent is obtained by a **clear affirmative action**. It is free, specific, informed, unconditional, and unambiguous, and is limited to the personal data necessary for the stated purpose, as required by Section 6 of the DPDP Act.\n\nASTEAI collects consent through:\n\n- **Registration Consent:** A clear, affirmative action during account creation — an unticked checkbox that you must actively select. We do not treat continued use of the Services as consent for processing that requires consent.\n- **Itemised Notice at the Point of Collection:** Before or at the time consent is requested, we present a notice describing the personal data to be collected, the specific purpose of processing, how you may withdraw consent, how you may exercise your rights, and how you may complain to the Data Protection Board of India.\n- **Granular Consent:** Separate, independently revocable consent for distinct processing purposes (marketing, analytics, optional AI features). Declining one does not require declining the others.\n- **Informed Consent:** Clear, plain-language notice available in **English and Hindi**, with other Eighth Schedule languages available on request.\n- **Cookie Consent:** A category-based cookie consent banner with accept/reject controls per category, and no non-essential cookies set before a choice is made.\n\n### 19.2 Consent Records\n\nWe maintain a record of every consent so that it can be demonstrated on request:\n\n- What was consented to (the specific purpose)\n- When consent was given (timestamp)\n- How consent was given (the mechanism and the version of the notice shown)\n- Whether and when consent was withdrawn\n\nConsent records are retained for the duration of the account relationship plus 24 months.\n\n### 19.3 Withdrawal of Consent\n\n- You may withdraw consent at any time through Account Settings, through the [Consent Preferences](https://asteai.com/consent-preferences) page, or by emailing privacy@asteai.com\n- Withdrawing consent is as easy as giving it\n- Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before the withdrawal\n- Where withdrawal makes it impossible for us to provide a particular service, we will tell you the consequences before processing the withdrawal\n- Consent withdrawal is processed within 7 business days\n\n### 19.4 Consent Managers\n\nThe DPDP Act provides for consent to be given, managed, and withdrawn through a registered Consent Manager. Where Consent Managers are operational and registered with the Data Protection Board of India, ASTEAI will accept and honour consent signals received through them. We will update this section when that mechanism becomes available to our users.\n\n---\n\n## 20. CHANGES TO THIS PRIVACY POLICY\n\n**Notification of Changes:**\n- Material changes communicated via email and platform notification\n- 30-day advance notice for changes affecting legal rights\n- Continued use after notice period constitutes acceptance\n- Previous versions of this policy are available on request from privacy@asteai.com\n\n**Version Control:**\n- All policy versions maintained with change logs\n- Effective date and version number clearly marked\n- Summary of changes provided with each update\n\n---\n\n## 21. CONTACT US & ESCALATION\n\nFor privacy requests, data deletion inquiries, security reports, or regulatory escalations, please contact our specialized teams:\n\n**General Privacy Inquiries:**  \n📧 privacy@asteai.com  \n🌐 Consent & Communication Preferences: https://asteai.com/consent-preferences\n\n**Data Protection Officer (GDPR/EU):**  \n📧 dpo@asteai.com\n\n**EU Representative (GDPR Article 27):**  \n📧 eu-representative@asteai.com\n\n**Grievance Officer (India — IT Rules 2021 & DPDP Act):**  \n👤 Rahul Yash Vardhan  \n📧 grievance@asteai.com  \n📞 +91 866 727 5560  \n📍 Startrit Infratech Pvt. Ltd., Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India - 600095  \n🕒 Working Hours: Monday to Friday, 10:00 AM to 6:00 PM IST  \nResponse Timeline: Acknowledgment within 24 hours, Resolution within 15 days\n\n**Nodal Contact Person (CERT-In Compliance):**  \n📧 security@asteai.com  \nAvailable 24/7 for cyber incident reporting\n\n**Security Incident Reporting:**  \n📧 security@asteai.com  \n🔐 PGP Key: Available on request from security@asteai.com\n\n**Quality & Service Issues:**  \n📧 quality@asteai.com\n\n**General Support:**  \n📧 supportasteai@startrit.com  \n📞 Support: (Business hours: Mon-Fri, 9 AM - 6 PM IST)\n\n**Corporate Address:**  \nStartrit Infratech Pvt. Ltd.  \nLegal & Compliance Department  \nChennai, Tamil Nadu, India - 600095  \n(Registered in Karnataka, India)\n\n**Regulatory Supervisory Authorities:**\n\nIf you are unsatisfied with our response to your privacy concerns, you may lodge a complaint with:\n\n- **European Union:** Your local Data Protection Authority (list: https://edpb.europa.eu/about-edpb/board/members_en)\n- **India:** Data Protection Board of India (https://www.dataprotection.gov.in) [When established]\n- **California, USA:** California Privacy Protection Agency (https://cppa.ca.gov)\n- **UK:** Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) (https://ico.org.uk)\n\n---\n\n## 22. TRANSPARENCY REPORT\n\nASTEAI is preparing an annual Transparency Report covering:\n- Government requests for user data\n- Law enforcement information requests\n- Data breach incidents and impact\n- Privacy rights requests statistics\n- Security incident summary\n- Platform integrity actions (account suspensions, fraud prevention)\n\nThe first edition has not yet been published. Until it is, you may request this information from compliance@asteai.com, and we will update this section with a permanent link once the report is available.\n\n---\n\n## 23. CERTIFICATION & COMPLIANCE STATUS\n\n**Certifications:**\n- ✅ ISO/IEC 27001:2022 (Information Security Management System) — certificate available on request\n\nASTEAI does not currently hold SOC 2, ISO 9001, ISO 14001, or ISO/IEC 42001 certification or attestation.\n\n**Regulatory Compliance Programme:**\n- Card payments are processed by Razorpay, a PCI-DSS compliant payment processor; ASTEAI does not store card numbers\n- GDPR (EEA, UK, Switzerland)\n- CCPA/CPRA (California, USA)\n- India DPDP Act 2023\n- IT Act 2000 & IT Rules 2021 (Intermediary obligations)\n\n**Compliance Audit Schedule:**\n- Internal ISMS Audits: At planned intervals, covering the full ISMS at least annually\n- ISO/IEC 27001 Surveillance Audits: Annually, by our certification body\n- ISO/IEC 27001 Recertification: Every three years\n- Penetration Testing: At least annually\n- Dependency Vulnerability Scanning: Continuous\n\n**Certification Verification:**\nRequest a copy of our ISO/IEC 27001 certificate: compliance@asteai.com\n\n---\n\n## 24. GLOSSARY OF TERMS\n\n**Personal Data:** Any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person.\n\n**Data Controller / Data Fiduciary:** The entity that determines the purposes and means of processing personal data (Startrit Infratech Pvt. Ltd., operating ASTEAI, for user account data).\n\n**Data Processor:** An entity that processes personal data on behalf of the controller (cloud providers, payment gateways).\n\n**Data Subject / Data Principal:** The individual to whom personal data relates.\n\n**Processing:** Any operation performed on personal data (collection, storage, use, disclosure, deletion).\n\n**Intermediary:** As defined under Section 2(1)(w) of the IT Act, 2000 — any person who, on behalf of another person, receives, stores, or transmits electronic records, or provides any service with respect to such records.\n\n**Certain Legitimate Uses:** The grounds enumerated in Section 7 of the DPDP Act on which personal data may be processed without separately obtained consent. The DPDP Act has no general \"legitimate interests\" basis.\n\n**Significant Data Fiduciary:** A Data Fiduciary notified as such by the Central Government under Section 10 of the DPDP Act, based on the volume and sensitivity of the personal data processed.\n\n**Consent Manager:** A person registered with the Data Protection Board of India who enables a Data Principal to give, manage, review, and withdraw consent through an accessible, transparent, and interoperable platform.\n\n**CERT-In:** The Indian Computer Emergency Response Team, the national nodal agency for responding to cyber security incidents.\n\n**Pseudonymization:** Processing personal data so it can no longer be attributed to a specific person without additional information.\n\n**Anonymization:** Irreversibly altering personal data so individuals cannot be identified.\n\n**Data Breach / Personal Data Breach:** Unauthorized or unlawful access, disclosure, alteration, or destruction of personal data.\n\n**Supervisory Authority:** Government body responsible for enforcing data protection laws.\n\n---\n\n## 25. GOVERNING LAW & JURISDICTION\n\nThis Privacy Policy is governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of **India**, without regard to conflict-of-law principles. The courts at **Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India** shall have jurisdiction over any dispute arising out of or in connection with this Privacy Policy, subject to the dispute resolution provisions of our Terms and Conditions, which continue to apply.\n\n**This does not remove your local protections.** Nothing in this section deprives you of the protection of the mandatory data protection law of your country of residence, or of your right to bring a complaint before, or seek a remedy from, your local supervisory authority:\n\n- **India:** Data Protection Board of India\n- **EEA / UK / Switzerland:** your local Data Protection Authority, including under GDPR Article 79\n- **California and other US states:** your state Attorney General or privacy agency\n\nWhere this Privacy Policy conflicts with a mandatory requirement of the data protection law applying to you, that requirement prevails to the extent of the conflict.\n\n**Relationship to our Terms and Conditions:** This Privacy Policy forms part of, and should be read together with, the ASTEAI Terms and Conditions. Where the two documents address the same subject, the more protective provision in respect of your personal data applies.\n\n---\n\n## ACKNOWLEDGMENT\n\nThis Privacy Policy & Compliance Framework represents ASTEAI's commitment to:\n- **Transparency:** Clear communication about data practices\n- **Accountability:** Taking responsibility for data protection\n- **Security:** Implementing robust technical and organizational measures\n- **Quality:** Delivering consistent, high-quality services\n- **Sustainability:** Reducing the environmental impact of our operations\n- **Trust:** Building lasting relationships with our users\n\nThis Privacy Policy is provided to you as notice of how we handle your personal data. Where we rely on your consent, that consent is collected separately and by clear affirmative action, as described in Section 19 — not by your use of the Services alone.\n\n---\n\n**Document Control:**\n- Document Owner: Data Protection Officer\n- Approval Authority: Executive Management & Legal Counsel\n- Next Review Date: December 31, 2026\n- Version: 2.3\n- Last Updated: October 6, 2026\n\n**Version History:**\n\n| Version | Date | Summary |\n|---------|------|---------|\n| 2.0 | June 30, 2026 | Baseline compliance framework |\n| 2.1 | July 16, 2026 | Intermediary status, Grievance Officer, DPDP Section 9, Consent Management, CERT-In notification, Brazil/Singapore coverage |\n| 2.2 | August 6, 2026 | Restored all v2.1 content omitted from the published document; disclosed sub-processors (Section 4.1); minimum age raised to 18 under DPDP Section 9; DPDP legal-basis column added to Section 17; breach notification aligned to DPDP Rules; consent mechanism restated under DPDP Section 6; anti-phishing, user security obligations, account-compromise procedure, and authentication/session disclosure added to Section 13; governing law added as Section 25 |\n| 2.3 | October 6, 2026 | Removed SOC 2, ISO 9001, ISO 14001 and ISO/IEC 42001 claims, which ASTEAI does not hold; replaced certificate placeholders in Section 23; restated Sections 6–9 to describe only controls ASTEAI operates (cloud-hosted infrastructure with no own data centres; removed multi-region failover, HSM, 24/7 SOC, code-coverage and fixed-uptime claims); aligned audit schedule with ISO/IEC 27001 surveillance cycle; linked customer Data Processing Agreement |\n\n> **Document control note:** Version 2.1, authored 16 July 2026, was not carried into the published document, which continued from an earlier 2.0 lineage. Version 2.2 restored that content. No version numbered below 2.3 should be treated as current.\n\n---\n\n*This document is maintained under the document control requirements of ASTEAI's ISO/IEC 27001 Information Security Management System.*\n";
